    "question": "Is a password manager actually safe to use, and which type should I choose?",
    "summary": "Password managers encrypt and store your credentials behind a single master password, and security experts broadly recommend them as one of the most effective ways to improve online security. Choosing between cloud-based, locally stored, self-hosted, or browser-built-in types depends on your…",
